{"id": "si-npg_NPG.67.62", "status": "ok", "meta": "Ole Peter Hansen Balling's 1880 portrait of Chester A. Arthur, the vice president who became the twenty-first president.", "about": "Chester A. Arthur became president in 1881 when James Garfield died, more than two months after being shot. Garfield's killer was a man seeking a government job, and that sharpened the argument over patronage. Arthur had long favored the spoils system. Yet he endorsed the Pendleton Civil Service Act, which created competitive examinations for some federal positions. Ole Peter Hansen Balling painted him in oil as a half-length figure with a full gray beard, a dark suit and an ornate stickpin in his tie. |||", "museum_record": "https://npg.si.edu/object/npg_NPG.67.62", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://npg.si.edu/object/npg_NPG.67.62"], "check": "clean"}
